# Working files, and why they are here rather than in a personal
# ~/.config/git/ignore: what keeps something out of this repository
# should travel with the repository.  A clone on another machine, or a
# contributor, gets the same protection.

# Reports, drafts, notes and the tooling that makes them.  Nothing in
# here is ever pushed; put a working file here rather than in the root.
/.donkey-local/

# Read by the coding assistant from the project root, so it cannot be
# moved into the directory above.
/CLAUDE.md

# Release notes, written for a GitHub release body and kept afterwards.
/release-*.md
